{
  "requirement": "Criterion code uses {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.read_source` for this operation.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `read_source.fn` says criterion code uses `ValidationContext.read_source` for the operation of reading a source node. The only behavior to test is that a criterion reaches source contents through that method, and that the method works through the framework.\n\n- `source_capable_validator_tracks_deterministic_reads_and_reuses_saved_results` in `project_sources.rs` runs a `Criterion` (the test's `ReadSource`). Its `execute` calls `cx.read_source(&OutlineId{...})`. The test runs it through `Validator::refresh_evidence`. It asserts the output equals the node's contents (\"first\"). It asserts the recorded dependency is `Dependency::Node(\"source-node\", fingerprint)`. It also asserts that the output follows changed contents (\"second\").\n- `direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns` calls `ValidationContext::read_source` directly. Unknown paths and unknown selectors return an \"unsupported source item\" error and record no dependency. A failing read returns an error and records no dependency. A successful read returns the contents and records one node dependency. The resulting record is current until the contents change, and then it is not.\n\nBecause the criterion's only access to source contents is the `cx.read_source` call, and the tests assert the observable results of that call, the tests cover the requirement. The behavior and inputs details belong to the sibling requirements `read_source.behavior` and `read_source.inputs`, and they are not assessed here. Both tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no gaps and no unacknowledged obligations.",
